<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lord's Resistance Army</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1987">1987</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as LRA</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lord's Resistance Army is a rebel group founded in northern Uganda in 1987 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-kony">Joseph Kony</a>, who claimed spiritual guidance and declared the aim of ruling by the Ten Commandments. Drawing on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acholi">Acholi</a> insurgency against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoweri-museveni">Yoweri Museveni</a>'s government, it waged a war of massacres, mutilation and the abduction of tens of thousands of children, displacing over a million people. After peace talks failed in 2008 it operated in the Congo, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-sudan">South Sudan</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-african-republic">Central African Republic</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lords-resistance-army.jpg" alt="Lord's Resistance Army" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UN Security Council · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LRAweapons.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
